t 14 weeks on the Dutch charts, peaking at 8 on 10 May 2014.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4103975","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":3323095,"name":"Chivv"},{"active":true,"id":5202280,"name":"Henkie T"},{"active":false,"id":5825292,"name":"Bryan K. Oduro"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4103975-SBMG","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.top-notch.nl/artiesten/sbmg","http://www.facebook.com/SBmoneygangg"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4487155/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4487155","image":"https://i.discogs.com/ujrnLwvVxSJs-jcZu5qyiyN4K7ZwA23N7oy_pLbL7yk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:599/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ0ODcx/NTUtMTU4NTE2NTQ3/Mi02MzEyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Cn2BmIo2KklVmir4manTC9Sc_t1D6PYcLaT-LNdayB0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ0ODcx/NTUtMTU4NTE2NTQ3/Mi02MzEyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Charlotte Dos Santos is a vocalist, composer and arranger – originally from Oslo, Norway and currently based in Berlin.\n*1990 Oslo, raised in Bærum, a small town outside Oslo, by her Norwegian mother and Brazilian father","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4487155","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4487155-Charlotte-Dos-Santos","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.instagram.com/charlottedossantos_/","http://soundcloud.com/charlottedossantos","https://twitter.com/charlottedossan","https://www.facebook.com/CharlotteDosSantosmusic/","","https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotte_Dos_Santos"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/44944/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"44944","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Y2P4gyJxtLjEfHzpP05Vfq9bNYQuGuEHvSJ86kG8410/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:449/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ0OTQ0/LTE3ODMwOTMyNjgt/NTc1Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/fsezWdIIGihT_NqayDxl3oAVPetBzhm_lD0YyCVNM4M/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ0OTQ0/LTE3ODMwOTMyNjgt/NTc1Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Born: February 11, 1974, Richmond, Virginia, U.S., and died: October 14, 2025, New York City, U.S., after short battle with cancer.\r\n\r\nHe was an American singer, songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer associated with the neo-soul movement circa the mid-90s. In his teens he won the amateur talent competition at Harlem's Apollo Theater three weeks in a row. His debut solo album, Brown Sugar (1995), received widespread acclaim and sold over two million copies. His next album, Voodoo (2000), debuted at number one on the US Billboard 200. Its lead single, \"Untitled (How Does It Feel),\" entered the R&B charts and won a Grammy for Best Male R&B Vocal; likewise, Voodoo won Best R&B Album. D'Angelo was hailed as the next Marvin Gaye by GQ in 2014. D'Angelo released his third studio album, Black Messiah, in 2014. The album was met with critical acclaim and fared well on music charts, peaking at number five on the US Billboard 200.\r\nFather of [a=Swayvo Twain].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:44944","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":683225,"name":"Michael Archer (2)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Angelo","D Angelo","D' Angelo","D'Aangelo","D'Angelo (aka D'Bonics)","D'angelo","D-Angelo","D. Angelo","D.Angelo","DAngelo","Dangelo","De Angelo","DeAngelo","Diangelo","DêAngelo","ディアンジェロ","狄安吉羅"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/44944-DAngelo","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/dangelo","https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKCWQOVUfdlDYX2_238_AeQ","https://www.instagram.com/thedangelo/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%27Angelo","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0195248/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4786421/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4786421","image":"https://i.discogs.com/eOtlUxgFjxpe22EQ0qjFU-IQNeDJyYO